ask23: extend cdx/lf66_compat.c with EHASH CRUD + IPR timer + fm_port_get_hwid

ask22 CI cleared the patch-apply step but modpost on cdx.ko reported
5 NEW unresolved symbols not yet covered by lf66_compat.c:

  ExternalHashTableAddKey
  ExternalHashTableDeleteKey
  ExternalHashSetDscpVlanpcpMapCfg
  ipr_update_timestamp
  fm_port_get_hwid

These follow the same lf-6.12.y vs lf-6.6.y SDK ABI gap pattern as the
ones already covered: lf-6.6.y SDK does not provide them, the cdx OOT
module references them on paths not exercised on the boot / cmm path:

- ExternalHash{Add,Delete}Key: callers in cdx_ehash.c, control_socket.c,
  cdx_dpa_ipsec.c. EHASH external-hash-table CRUD; SDK-side hash always
  in-MURAM in lf-6.6.y, the external-table path is unreachable.
- ExternalHashSetDscpVlanpcpMapCfg: cdx_ehash.c IPR-related QoS map
  config; pairs with ExternalHashGetDscpVlanpcpMapCfg already stubbed.
- ipr_update_timestamp: cdx_reassm.c calls per kernel tick; SDK-side
  IPR is not exercised, no-op is safe.
- fm_port_get_hwid: devman.c uses for iface_info->eth_info.hardwarePortId
  (informational only, fed back to userspace on a query path).

Bringing the lf66_compat.c stub TU from 11 to 16 stubs total. None
reachable on the boot/cmm path; modpost gets external linkage for
each via EXPORT_SYMBOL.

